""" Sorry "" was one of the first tracks developed for Confessions on a Dance Floor , along with "" Hung Up "" and "" Future Lovers "" . It was also the one which took the most time to finish because Madonna "" thought it was too melodramatic and could never decide when it was right . "" The songs were developed with a remixed perspective in mind . Madonna commented that , "" Whenever I make records , I often like the remixes better than the original ones . [ ... ] So I thought , screw that . I 'm going to start from that perspective "" . She promoted the album at the dance party "" Misshapes "" held at Luke & Leroy 's nightclub in Greenwich Village , invited by Junior Sanchez to take over the DJ booth where she mixed "" Hung Up "" with "" Sorry "" . Musically , "" Sorry "" is an uptempo dance song containing layers of beats and strong vocal on the chorus . It is set in common time with a moderately fast dance groove tempo of 132 beats per minute . Composed in the key of C minor , Madonna 's vocal range spans from F3 to G4 . It follows the chord progression of E ♭ – Cm – A ♭ – B ♭ during the spoken introduction . It then changes to Fm – Gm @-@ Cm in the chorus , while continuing in A ♭ – Cm – A ♭ – Fm in the intermediate verses , ultimately ending in repeated lines of "" I 've heard it all before "" .",0,wikipedia_val,BENIGN,0af052ac3c93,False,False,False,False,False,False
